=== test_aba_demo ===
=== ABA Bug Demonstration ===

Initial: top → A(1) → B(2) → C(3) → sentinel
[T1] Read top=A(1), next=B(2)
[T2] Popped A(1). Stack: top → B → C
[T2] Popped B(2). Stack: top → C. T2 OWNS B(2).
[T2] Pushed A(1) back. Stack: top → A → C
[T2] ABA ready: top == node_a (same physical pointer)
[T1] CAS(top, A, B) = true — ABA BUG TRIGGERED!
[T1] top is now B(2), but T2 already owns B!

*** ABA BUG CONFIRMED ***
CAS succeeded because node_a is the same physical pointer,
even though the stack structure changed underneath.
Node B is in the stack AND owned by T2 — double use!

HP prevents this: T1's hazard pointer on A blocks T2
from recycling A, so A can't reappear at top.
EBR prevents this: A stays in limbo until all domains
have advanced past the retirement epoch.
>>> test_aba_demo: PASS <<<

